- <h1>The Best Immersive Experiences in Barcelona: A Complete Guide (2026)</h1>
- <div class="article-meta"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/marvynhalfon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">Marvyn Halfon</a> &middot; Co-founder, SABDA Studio<br><span style="opacity:.72">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-08-13">August 13, 2026</time></span></div>
-<p>Barcelona has become one of Europe's top cities for immersive experiences. 360° projections, spatial audio, interactive installations, and spaces where you don't watch the art, you're inside it. But not all immersive experiences are the same, and the gap between them is bigger than you'd think.</p>
-<p>This guide compares every major option, explains what to expect from each, and helps you pick based on what you're actually looking for.</p>
+ <h1>Immersive Experiences in Barcelona: What's Open and What's Closed (2026)</h1>
+ <div class="article-meta"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/marvynhalfon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">Marvyn Halfon</a> &middot; Co-founder, SABDA Studio<br><span style="opacity:.72">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-17">October 17, 2026</time></span></div>
+<p>Looking for an immersive experience in Barcelona and not sure what is still running? This page is the status check. Immersive shows in Barcelona open and close every few months, and old listings stay online long after a show has gone, so below is every immersive experience people search for, marked as open, finished or coming soon, with dates and prices checked on each venue's official website.</p>
+<p>If you want our ranked recommendations with verdicts instead, see <a href="/blog/best-immersive-experiences-barcelona/">the 11 best immersive experiences in Barcelona</a>. One venue on this page is ours, and we say so where it appears.</p>
 <hr />
-<h2>What "immersive" means</h2>
-<p>An immersive experience is anything where the environment surrounds you and you're part of it. Instead of observing from outside. In practice, this ranges from large-scale projection exhibitions (passive. You walk, look, absorb) to spaces where you actively move, breathe, or dance inside the art (participatory).</p>
-<p>The key difference: passive immersion is impressive. Participatory immersion is transformative.</p>
+<h2>Open now</h2>
+<p><strong>SABDA's new immersive show (Eixample): open from 17 October 2026.</strong> Full disclosure: SABDA is our venue. SABDA's new immersive show is a 25 minute journey through four worlds of life on Earth, made in Unreal Engine and projected across the four walls of a 360° room with Dolby Atmos sound, for 25 people per session at C/ Muntaner 83B in the Eixample. It runs on Fridays, Saturdays and Sundays, at €20 for adults and €12 for children, including a welcome glass of cava or juice in SABDA Café. There is no headset. Details on <a href="/exhibitions/">SABDA's exhibitions page</a>.</p>
+<p><strong>Gaudí at Casa Batlló: open.</strong> Every ticket includes the Gaudí Cube, a six-sided LED room with Refik Anadol's "Gaudí Dreams", plus augmented reality during the visit. From €29, children up to 12 free, about 1 hour 15 minutes. <a href="https://www.casabatllo.es/en/experience/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">casabatllo.es</a></p>
+<p><strong>Gaudí at Codi Gaudí (Espai Imagina): open until 8 January 2027.</strong> A mixed and virtual reality experience about the buildings Gaudí never built, at Av. Diagonal 177. Adults from €12.50 on Mondays, closed on Tuesdays, about 70 minutes. <a href="https://espai-imagina.com/exposicions/codi-gaudi-experiencia-inedita/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">espai-imagina.com</a></p>
+<p><strong>Dalí Boulevard Cibernètic: open.</strong> An immersive Dalí experience in Casa Amatller, Passeig de Gràcia 41. From €15 on weekdays and €18 at weekends, about 75 minutes.</p>
+<p><strong>IKONO: open.</strong> More than ten playful, photo-friendly immersive rooms on the third floor of the Arenas shopping centre at Plaça d'Espanya, daily from 12:00 to 19:00. IKONO has moved: older listings give an address in Barceloneta, which is out of date. <a href="https://ikono.global/en/barcelona" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ikono.global</a></p>
+<p><strong>White Rabbit: open.</strong> Ten immersive rooms about Catalan traditions by local artists, at Passeig de Gràcia 55. From €16, 60 to 90 minutes.</p>
+<p><strong>Moco Museum: open.</strong> Contemporary and street art with a digital and immersive collection, at Carrer de Montcada 25 in the Born. From €14.95, children up to 6 free.</p>
+<p><strong>Antarctica Experience (GIGA, Arenas): open.</strong> From €12.90, under-3s free, 45 to 75 minutes. No end date published.</p>
+<p><strong>Iniesta Experience: open until 10 January 2027.</strong> In the former IMAX on Moll d'Espanya, from €18, about 90 minutes.</p>
+<p><strong>Museum of Banksy: open.</strong> Carrer Trafalgar 34, €14, under-6s free.</p>
 <hr />
-<h2>The major immersive spaces in Barcelona</h2>
-<h3>SABDA. Participatory immersive wellness</h3>
-<p>If you're looking for immersive experience barcelona, this guide covers what actually matters. <a href="https://sabdastudio.com/classes/">SABDA</a> is the only space in Barcelona where wellness and immersive technology converge. A 360° projection room with Dolby Atmos spatial audio (cinema-grade speakers built into every wall and ceiling, subwoofers underneath) where classes run in yoga, <a href="/classes/pilates/">pilates</a>, sound healing, breathwork, ecstatic dance, and ice bath.</p>
-<p><strong>What makes it different:</strong> You don't watch, you move, breathe, and participate inside the art. Visuals are custom-designed for each class. A vinyasa session has abstract landscapes that flow with the rhythm. A sound healing session has living geometry that pulses with Tibetan singing bowls. Spatial audio wraps around you from every direction.</p>
-<p><strong>Best for:</strong> People who want to feel something, not just see something pretty. Anyone curious about the intersection of art, technology, and wellness.</p>
-<p><strong>Price:</strong> From €18/class. <a href="/pricing.html">3 classes for €50</a>.
-<strong>Frequency:</strong> 42+ classes per week + special events.
-<strong>Where:</strong> C/Muntaner 83B, Eixample.</p>
-<h3>IDEAL, Centre d'Arts Digitals</h3>
-<p>Barcelona's large-scale immersive exhibition space. Housed in a former industrial warehouse in Poblenou, IDEAL projects artwork across walls, floor, and ceiling. Exhibitions rotate every 6-12 months, check the current programme. It's passive, you walk, sit, look, and let it surround you.</p>
-<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Families, tourists, anyone who wants a spectacular visual experience without active participation.</p>
-<p><strong>Price:</strong> ~€15-18.
-<strong>Where:</strong> C/Dr. Trueta, 196, Poblenou.</p>
-<h3>Moco Museum</h3>
-<p>Digital and contemporary art in an 18th-century palace in the Born. More gallery than immersive experience, but with interactive rooms that offer genuine moments of immersion. The permanent collection features major contemporary artists, and temporary exhibitions rotate.</p>
-<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Contemporary art fans. People who want photos for Instagram (the museum is designed for it).</p>
-<p><strong>Price:</strong> ~€16.
-<strong>Where:</strong> C/Montcada, 25, Born.</p>
-<h3>IKONO</h3>
-<p>A sensory experience space designed primarily for photos. Themed rooms with different textures, colours, and interactive elements. Each room is a production set disguised as an "experience."</p>
-<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Content creators. Friend groups who want a fun, photogenic activity.</p>
-<p><strong>Price:</strong> ~€16-20.
-<strong>Where:</strong> Passeig de Joan de Borbó, 80, Barceloneta.</p>
-<h3>Candlelight Concerts (Fever)</h3>
-<p>Classical music and soundtrack concerts by candlelight in atmospheric venues like churches and historic buildings. The format is "immersive" in the atmospheric sense. The environment contributes to the experience, but there's no projection technology or spatial audio.</p>
-<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Couples, date nights, anyone who wants a lovely evening without complexity.</p>
-<p><strong>Price:</strong> From ~€15.</p>
+<h2>Finished or not running</h2>
+<p><strong>Pompeii (IDEAL Montjuïc): finished.</strong> "The Last Days of Pompeii" closed on 21 September 2026. No replacement has been announced.</p>
+<p><strong>IDEAL Poblenou: no programme.</strong> IDEAL's website now lists only its Montjuïc venue, with nothing announced after Pompeii. Check <a href="https://idealbarcelona.com/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">idealbarcelona.com</a> before planning around it.</p>
+<p><strong>Mundo Pixar: finished in Barcelona.</strong> The official Mundo Pixar website no longer lists Barcelona among its cities.</p>
+<p><strong>Eonarium: finished.</strong> Its Barcelona page reads "Exhibition Finished".</p>
+<p><strong>Sorolla: not confirmed.</strong> No Sorolla immersive exhibition is confirmed in Barcelona.</p>
+<p><strong>Van Gogh: not running.</strong> No Van Gogh exhibition or immersive experience is running or announced in Barcelona.</p>
+<p><strong>Tutankhamun and Egypt: finished.</strong> The Tutankhamun show at IDEAL closed in June 2024.</p>
+<p><strong>Balloon Story: finished</strong> on 4 October 2026.</p>
