+<h2>Coming soon</h2>
+<p><strong>MIRA Digital Arts Festival, 6 and 7 November 2026.</strong> Audiovisual shows and 360° fulldome pieces at Fira Montjuïc. Day pass €60, full pass €110.</p>
+<p><strong>LOOP Barcelona, 10 to 21 November 2026.</strong> Video art across museums, galleries and cinemas.</p>
+<p><strong>Llum BCN, 5 to 7 February 2027.</strong> The city's free light art festival, in Poblenou.</p>
 <hr />
-<h2>Which to choose</h2>
-<p><strong>If you want to feel something:</strong> <a href="https://sabdastudio.com/classes/">SABDA</a>. Active participation (moving, breathing, lying still) combined with total immersion produces experiences that go beyond visual. You leave different from how you arrived.</p>
-<p><strong>If you want to see something spectacular:</strong> IDEAL. The projections are visually impressive. It's the option for "I want to walk in, look around, and say wow."</p>
-<p><strong>If you want photos:</strong> IKONO or Moco Museum. Both optimised for visual content.</p>
-<p><strong>If you want a lovely evening:</strong> Candlelight Concerts. Simple, atmospheric, no complications.</p>
-<p><strong>If you want contemporary art with immersive moments:</strong> Moco Museum. Strong permanent collection plus interactive elements.</p>
+<h2>Immersive dining in Barcelona</h2>
+<p>We could not verify a public immersive dining show currently running in Barcelona. SABDA's 360° room hosts immersive dinners for private groups and events; see <a href="/hire/">private events</a>.</p>
+<hr />
+<h2>What "immersive" actually means</h2>
+<p>"Immersive" now covers everything from a room with a projector to a headset. In practice, Barcelona's immersive experiences fall into four formats: headset VR (Codi Gaudí), projection around you in a room (SABDA, Antarctica Experience), LED screens (Casa Batlló's Gaudí Cube), and walk-through rooms built for photos and play (IKONO, White Rabbit, Moco's digital rooms). None is better by default. VR gives you the most freedom of movement, projection rooms let you share the moment with the people next to you, and walk-through rooms are the easiest with children.</p>
+<hr />
+<h2>FAQ</h2>
+<p><strong>What immersive experiences are open in Barcelona right now?</strong>
+Casa Batlló, Codi Gaudí, Dalí Boulevard Cibernètic, IKONO, White Rabbit, Moco Museum, Antarctica Experience, Iniesta Experience and the Museum of Banksy. SABDA's new immersive show opens on 17 October 2026.</p>
+<p><strong>Is there a Gaudí immersive experience in Barcelona?</strong>
+Yes, two. Casa Batlló includes the Gaudí Cube with every ticket, and Codi Gaudí at Espai Imagina is a mixed and virtual reality experience about Gaudí's unbuilt buildings, open until 8 January 2027.</p>
+<p><strong>Is the Pompeii immersive exhibition still on in Barcelona?</strong>
+No. It closed at IDEAL Montjuïc on 21 September 2026.</p>
+<p><strong>Is there a Sorolla or Van Gogh immersive experience in Barcelona?</strong>
+No. Neither is running or confirmed in Barcelona.</p>
+<p><strong>Where is IKONO Barcelona now?</strong>
+On the third floor of the Arenas shopping centre, Gran Via 373, at Plaça d'Espanya. It is open daily from 12:00 to 19:00.</p>
+<p><strong>How much is SABDA's new immersive show?</strong>
+€20 for adults and €12 for children, including a welcome glass of cava or juice in SABDA Café. It lasts 25 minutes and runs on Fridays, Saturdays and Sundays.</p>
 <hr />
-<h2>Before you go</h2>
-<p>If you only have time for one immersive experience in Barcelona, choose based on what you want to take away: a photo, a visual memory, or a physical transformation. All three options exist. Only one changes how you feel when you leave.</p>
-<p><a href="https://momence.com/m/443935" target="_self" rel="noopener noreferrer">3 immersive classes at SABDA for €50</a>. Yoga, sound healing, breathwork, or ecstatic dance inside 360° projections with Dolby Atmos spatial audio.</p>
